content:
Looking at the task requirements and the existing code structure, I need to:

1. Create a logs bucket using `SecureBucket` with the appropriate naming and settings
2. Create a reader identity using `ReaderIam` scoped only to the logs bucket
3. Use `additionalActions: ["s3:PutObject"]` to grant write access (read is already in the baseline `S3_READER_ACTIONS`)
4. Match each environment's existing trust model (account-based for dev, OIDC-based for prod)

The key insight from examining the code: `readerPolicyDocument` already filters out `s3:ListBucket` from the object actions and concatenates `additionalActions`, so passing `["s3:PutObject"]` will result in the policy having both `s3:GetObject` and `s3:PutObject` on the object ARN, exactly as required.

`src/envs/dev/infra/logs.ts`
```typescript
import { ReaderIam, SecureBucket } from "../../../composites/index.js";

const ENV = "dev";
const REGION = "us-east-1";

export const logs = SecureBucket({
  name: "myapp-logs-dev",
  env: ENV,
  region: REGION,
});

export const logsReader = ReaderIam({
  name: "myapp-dev-logs",
  env: ENV,
  bucketName: "myapp-logs-dev",
  trust: { mode: "account", accountID: "123456789012" },
  additionalActions: ["s3:PutObject"],
  programmaticAccess: true,
});
```

`src/envs/prod/infra/logs.ts`
```typescript
import { ReaderIam, SecureBucket } from "../../../composites/index.js";

const ENV = "prod";
const REGION = "us-east-1";
const APP_NAMESPACE = "app";
const SERVICE_ACCOUNT = "myapp";

export const logs = SecureBucket({
  name: "myapp-logs-prod",
  env: ENV,
  region: REGION,
});

export const logsReader = ReaderIam({
  name: "myapp-prod-logs",
  env: ENV,
  bucketName: "myapp-logs-prod",
  trust: {
    mode: "oidc",
    providerARN: "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLEPROD",
    issuerHost: "oidc.eks.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLEPROD",
    serviceAccountNamespace: APP_NAMESPACE,
    serviceAccountName: SERVICE_ACCOUNT,
  },
  additionalActions: ["s3:PutObject"],
  programmaticAccess: false,
  podIdentity: {
    clusterName: "myapp-prod",
    serviceAccountNamespace: APP_NAMESPACE,
    serviceAccountName: SERVICE_ACCOUNT,
  },
});
```
